# Line-ending policy
#
# The repo's build gates are byte-exact across machines:
#   - scripts/lint-webui.sh compares the committed WebMod/bundle.js byte-for-byte
#     against a fresh tsc compilation,
#   - scripts/package.sh promises two zips of one commit hash identically
#     regardless of build machine,
#   - every script/*.sh and the Makefile break outright when run with CRLF
#     endings under bash.
# Normalize all text files to LF in the index and force LF in working trees on
# every platform, so a checkout on Windows or macOS cannot corrupt those
# contracts the way core.autocrlf=true would.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary artifacts git must never touch (explicit even where detection already
# gets it right).
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.dll binary
*.tar.gz binary
*.tgz binary
*.jar binary
